---
import LegalShell from '../components/LegalShell.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalShell
  title="Privacy Notice (POPIA) — Basebond Solutions"
  heading="Privacy Notice"
  updated="21 November 2026"
  path="/privacy"
  description="How Basebond Solutions collects, uses and protects personal information in line with the Protection of Personal Information Act, 2013."
  intro="This notice explains what personal information we collect, why we collect it, and the rights you have under the Protection of Personal Information Act 4 of 2013 (POPIA)."
>
  <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {site.legalName} is the responsible party for the personal information described in
    this notice. Our Information Officer can be reached at
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Enquiry details</strong> — your name, business name, email address, phone number, the service you are interested in and the message you send us.</li>
    <li><strong>Newsletter details</strong> — your email address, if you choose to subscribe.</li>
    <li><strong>Client records</strong> — where you become a client, the financial, payroll, tax and (for practice clients) patient-billing information necessary to deliver the service.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical information</strong> — standard server logs generated when you visit the site, including IP address, browser type and pages requested.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Why we process it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To respond to your enquiry and provide a quotation.</li>
    <li>To deliver accounting, tax, payroll, billing and related services you engage us for.</li>
    <li>To meet our obligations under tax, company and anti-money-laundering legislation.</li>
    <li>To send the newsletter you asked for, which you can unsubscribe from at any time.</li>
    <li>To keep the website secure and diagnose technical problems.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Lawful basis</h2>
  <p>
    We process enquiry and client information because it is necessary to perform a
    contract with you or to take steps at your request before entering into one. We
    process records required by tax and company law because we have a legal obligation
    to do so. We send the newsletter on the basis of your consent, which you may withdraw
    at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information. We share it only where necessary: with SARS and
    CIPC where a filing requires it, with your accounting or practice-management software
    provider, with our email delivery provider, and with professional advisers where
    required. Where a service provider processes information on our behalf, we require
    appropriate confidentiality and security commitments.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Cross-border processing</h2>
  <p>
    Some of our service providers, including our website host and email delivery
    provider, may process information on servers outside South Africa. Where this
    happens, we rely on the protections permitted under section 72 of POPIA, including
    contractual safeguards and the provider's security commitments.
  </p>

  <h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiry records are kept for as long as needed to deal with the enquiry and any
    follow-up. Client records are retained for the periods required by tax and company
    legislation, which is generally five years from the end of the relevant tax year,
    and longer where a legal dispute or audit is pending. Newsletter details are kept
    until you unsubscribe.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under POPIA you may ask us to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>confirm whether we hold personal information about you, and provide a copy;</li>
    <li>correct or delete information that is inaccurate, irrelevant, excessive or unlawfully obtained;</li>
    <li>stop processing your information for direct marketing;</li>
    <li>withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Requests should be sent to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We may
    ask you to verify your identity before acting on a request. If you believe we have
    not handled your information lawfully, you may complain to the Information Regulator
    (South Africa) at <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">inforegulator.org.za</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Security</h2>
  <p>
    Access to client information is limited to the practitioners assigned to your file.
    Documents are stored in access-controlled cloud folders, transmitted over encrypted
    connections, and handled under written confidentiality undertakings. We review access
    when a practitioner leaves an engagement.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The site uses only what is necessary to function. See our
    <a href="/cookies">cookie notice</a> for detail.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this notice when our processing activities change. The date at the top
    of this page shows when it was last revised.
  </p>
</LegalShell>
